*1) Facial expressions (smiling, neutral, frowning)**  \nIn close-up frames (e.g., 4–7), attendees are seen clapping, with many displaying neutral to pleased expressions. Some are smiling faintly, while others maintain formal, attentive neutral faces. There is no visible frowning or overt signs of boredom (e.g., yawning, glazed eyes, slumped brows). The expressions are consistent with formal, respectful engagement.\n\n**2) Body language/posture (relaxed, attentive, slouching)**  \nAudience members are seated upright, facing the stage. Posture is consistently formal and attentive, not slouched or relaxed in a casual manner. In wide shots (e.g., 8–18, 19–29), the crowd is uniformly oriented toward the stage, indicating sustained focus.\n\n**3) Audience engagement (applauding, watching attentively, looking distracted)**  \nFrames 4–7 show active applause, indicating high engagement. In wider shots (8–29), while not all are clapping, the entire audience is visually oriented toward the stage. No significant distractions (e.g., people looking at phones, talking, or looking away) are visible. The engagement is consistent and sustained.\n\n**4) Overall atmosphere (festive, formal, somber)**  \nThe setting is grand and formal — black-tie attire, ornate hall, ceremonial stage setup. The atmosphere is dignified and celebratory (as expected at a Nobel Prize ceremony), not festive like a party, nor somber like a memorial. It is a solemn celebration of achievement.\n\n**5) Interactions between people (conversing, nodding, ignoring)**  \nIn close-ups (e.g., 4–7), some individuals are seen nodding or turning slightly to acknowledge neighbors, but no prolonged conversations or social distractions are visible. Most are focused forward, indicating respectful, minimal interaction appropriate for a formal ceremony.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence and Context**  \nAcross all 29 frames, spanning different moments of the ceremony (awards being presented, applause, seated listening), the mood remains consistently formal, respectful, and engaged. There is no temporal shift toward boredom or disinterest. Even during quieter moments (e.g., 8–18), the audience remains attentive.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion**  \nThe mood of the people at the scene is best described as **attentive, respectful, and formally engaged** — not bored or uninterested. The ceremonial context, attire, posture, and active applause all contradict the notion of boredom.\n\nTherefore, **answer '2' (Bored, not interested) is incorrect**."}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1063.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1064.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1065.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1066.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1067.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1068.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1069.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1070.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1071.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1072.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1073.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1103.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1104.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1105.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1106.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1107.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1108.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1109.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8NHmfpkxTSw/frames/frame_1110.jpg, /mnt/ssd